I think it's a cute idea.  It could be like a shop - as the shopkeeper
will not allow you to enter if you are invisible or wielding a
pick-axe, the priest/ess would not allow you to enter if you were
wearing a hat, etc.  If you didn't want to follow the rules, you could
teleport in, and like the shopkeeper then the priest wouldn't be able
to do anything about it (but could still stand in front of the door to
prevent you from leaving - well, I guess that wouldn't make much
sense).  You could also get a warning for eating inside the temple,
just as the guards in the mine town warn you not to drink from
fountains or (usually) pick locks before they try to kill you.

In any case I don't think this idea should be taken TOO far - it is
always so nice to find a temple, especially a co-aligned one with no
priest/ess to get angry and no danger from monsters.  I wouldn't want
to make them too inaccessible - they're rare enough as it is in many
games.

